# 9. AUTOMATIC CLOUD SYNCHRONIZATION – PHONE A TO PHONE B

The application must work across multiple devices.

Example:

Phone A:
- Admin creates a quotation.
- Employee marks attendance.
- Site Manager uploads project photographs.
- Accountant records a payment.

All these changes must be saved to the cloud database.

Phone B:
- The same authorized user logs in.
- Application fetches the latest permitted records from the cloud.
- All relevant information appears automatically.

Requirements:

1. Fetch cloud records after successful login.
2. Save records directly to the cloud.
3. Update cloud records after edits.
4. Support real-time synchronization where appropriate.
5. Refresh screens after successful updates.
6. Prevent duplicate records.
7. Handle simultaneous updates safely.
8. Preserve data after logout.
9. Preserve data after reinstalling the application.
10. Make data available on another authorized device.

If a user creates data on Phone A, the same account must be able to see that data on Phone B.

Do not show local unsynchronized data as if it were saved successfully.

